WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
Two masses exert forces on each other.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.020
So do two electric charges.

3
00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.910
Both forces are inverse-square:
as the distance grows,

4
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.660
they fade the same way.

5
00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.470
Around a single mass or a single charge,
the field lines spread out radially,

6
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.140
the same pattern.

7
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.490
So are they really the
same force in disguise?

8
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.260
And if not, where do they part company?

9
00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.490
In this mission, you'll set the
gravitational and electric force laws side by

10
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:28.320
side.

11
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:32.040
Then you'll compare the two forces
between a pair of electrons.

12
00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.680
Your mission: find where gravitational
and electric forces part company.
